On Nov 22, 6:02 pm, Jorgen Grahn <grahn+n...@snipabacken.se> wrote:

> Not in most of my games. More like half a dozen. And I go after every
> nymph,

Really?

Huh.

I generally meet about 2 nymphs per level when playing through
initially,
plus more whenever I backtrack through levels I'd previously explored.
About half of them drop potions.

> and use those potions only to find Ludios.

I've been using a pick-axe for that.

Vaults are generally easy to find, because there's usually
a very obvious blank space where *something* ought to be,
plus you hear the guard patrolling every few moves so you
definitely know to look on that level.

Then again, when I finally get levitation I usually go for
Medusa first and then the Castle and get around to Fort
Ludios subsequently, so by that time I'm usually into
the middle game and don't have any particular need to
hurry, so I can afford to dig corridors across the obvious
blank spaces even on levels that may not have a vault.

> Later I might use them to make Gehennom less boring,

I use wands of digging for that.  I save one or two in my
stash, but digging is one of the more common wands,
so I generally can spare several of them for opening up
what would otherwise be dead ends in the maze levels
and thus avoid much backtracking.

> or turn them into extra water.

By the time I get my ascension kit assembled, I
usually have 15-20 holy water in my bag of holding
and 2-3 times that much stashed.  Most of that comes
from unicorn-horn-clearable potions (which avoids
overtaxing the fountains) and extremely plentiful
otherwise useless ones, of which object detection
is chief.  I save at least one sickness for dipping
my big fat stack of blessed +7 projectiles (darts
or whatnot) for the ascension kit.  Speed and
healing and extra healing and enlightenment and
levitation all go into alchemy.  Full healing and
any gain energy that are left after alchemy get
blessed and either quaffed or saved.  Gain level
get either blessed and quaffed or cursed and
saved.  Booze either gets saved for confusion
purposes or canceled, and if I have more fruit
juice than I can use for nutritional purposes at
can't-stop-to-eat times I sometimes dip a stack
of that for water.  See invisible is another one
that I sometimes dip for water.  Oil usually gets
used up in lamps, unless I happen to have found
a better light source (e.g., one game there was
an A pretty early in the Mines for some reason,
which dropped a blessed Sunsword, and I was
already skilled in longsword, so naturally I
rustrpoofed and enchanted that baby and used
it for the duration; I'm not counting on having
THAT happen every game).


